On Feb 19, 3:58 am, pp <p...@mm.org> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> Can anyone please tell me what are the difference between dupatch and
> setld? they are seem to be dealing with the same thing -
> install/deinstall software in tru64.
>
> Thanks
> P

Basically, dupatch is used exclusively for installing/removing patch
kits and setld is used to exclusively install/remove software
subsets.  While dupatch actually uses setld to install/remove patches,
it is never recommended to use setld explicitly to install/remove
patches (in fact, you will more than likely get errors if you try to
use setld to install/remove patches).  Also, not all software requires
the use of dupatch or setld to be installed (alot of the freeware on
the internet, for example, does not come bundled in a setld-based
format; often such software will come with a README explaining how to
instal/configure it).  It's best to just remember that dupatch is for
patch subsets, setld is not :-)

