On Feb 19, 2:54 am, Pet <p...@modulus.org> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I remembered there are different ways to install patches in Tru64
> (4.0E/F and 5.0). Can anyone please tell me what are different methods
> of installing patches in Tru64?
>
> Your suggestion is very well appreciated.
> Thanks
> D

I believe that 4.0D was the first release of Tru64 to use the
"dupatch" utility to install patches; all versions after 4.0D use
dupatch exclusively to install patches.  Prior to 4.0D, patch kits
came in tar files and the modules in them more or less had to manually
be moved into place before a kernel rebuild (doconfig) and system
reboot was performed.

Patch kits today usually come in 3 forms:

1.  Aggregate (official release) kits
2.  Early Release kits (those not contained in an aggregate kit)
3.  Customer-Specific kits (those developed by Engineering for a
specific customer problem)

The dupatch utility, more often than not, is used to install all of
these kit types.  The README's that accompany the patch kits should
contain applicable installation instructions.

More information on patch kits can be found here:

http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/patch/naming/TITLE.HTM (Patch Kit
naming)
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/unix/EarlyReleasePatch-download.html (Early
Release Patches)
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/patch/roadmap.html (Aggregate Kit
Roadmap)
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/patch/ (Aggregate Kit Release Notes/
Downloads/etc.)

