On Feb 16, 4:13 pm, Pet <p...@modulus.org> wrote:
> Hi,
>
> I lost the installation manual of tru64 (4.0F and 5.1),
> can anyone please tell me how to boot the system into maintainance mode
> in which you can see all hardware configuration? it is not the single
> user mode I am after.
>
> Thank you in advance
> S

You can see your hardware configuration from the SRM (>>>) prompt.
This is console mode (run-level 0), so you can do one of the following
to get there from multi-user mode:

# init 0 (runs the init transition scripts to run-level 0 with no
warning to users)
#shutdown -h now (halts the system right away without running the
transition scripts, but does warn users via "wall")

Once at console mode, there's a number of commands to check the HW
config:

>>>show config (hw config)
>>>show dev (device info)
>>>show fru (field replace-able unit info)
>>>show power (power-related info)
>>>show version (report firmware version)
>>>help (to get help info)


